127:   <h1 id="introduction"> <a href="#contents" class="contentArrow">&#9650;</a> Introduction </h1>
128:   <p>SQ MixPad allows you to control the SQ digital audio mixer over a network connection.</p>
129:   <p>Three devices running SQ MixPad can be used alongside the SQ itself to provide a total of four screens on which to view and control parameters.</p>
130:   <p>Each instance of SQ-MixPad and the SQ firmware <u>must</u> share the same feature release number.</p>
131:   <p>i.e. <br />
132:     SQ firmware V1.<span class="info">5</span>.4 and SQ MixPad V1.<span class="info">5</span>.1 = compatible. <br />
133:     SQ firmware V1.<span class="info">3</span>.2 and SQ MixPad V1.<span class="info">5</span>.2 = <u>not</u> compatible.</p>
134:   <p>For this reason, we suggest you turn automatic updates for SQ MixPad on mobile devices <u>OFF</u>, so you can update the firmware and app manually to guarantee
135:     compatibility.</p>
136:   <p>Check <a href="http://www.allen-heath.com/" target="_new">www.allen-heath.com</a> for the latest SQ firmware release and reference
137:     guide. <br />
138:   </p>
139:   <p>This guide presumes you are familiar with the operation and setup of the SQ itself and is intended as an accompaniment to
140:     the SQ Reference Guide. </p>
141:   <h1 id="connectRouter"> <a href="#contents" class="contentArrow">&#9650;</a> Connecting MixPad to an SQ </h1>
142:   <p>We recommend using a dedicated dual-band router or access point with auto channel setting to avoid interruptions and dropouts that can be caused by other devices in the area or other connections using bandwidth on the same network.<br>
143:     Most 'off-the-shelf' routers will work, though you will need to choose one that is suitable for
144:     the situations it will be used in. For example - you will find that long distance wireless use in a venue with many other
145:     wireless devices (e.g. mobile phones) around will require a better router than if you were just connecting at home.<br>
146:     Position of the router or access point will also make a difference, and it is usually best to get the aerial high up, away from walls or surfaces and within line of sight of the device running MixPad.</p>
147:   <ul>
148:     <li>The system runs on a Local Area Network (LAN), no internet connection is required or provided.</li>
149:     <li>Use a standard network cable to connect the <strong>Network</strong> port on the rear of the SQ to a <strong>LAN</strong> port on the router. If you are following router instructions, you can connect the SQ in the same way
150:       as you would connect a computer. If your router is new, it may need to be set up using a computer prior to use with the
151:       SQ.</li>
152:     <li>By default, the SQ is set to automatically receive an address using DHCP. By using DHCP on the SQ <em>and</em> the remote device, compatible IP addresses should be assigned.</li>
153:     <li>If DHCP is selected, but no address is received, the SQ will auto-assign an address.</li>
154:     <li>If you are not using DHCP and instead use static IP addresses on the SQ and device, make sure
155:       they are in the same range and share the same first 3 values. e.g. 192.168.1.***<br>
156:       Be careful not to assign an address  that is already in use on the network.</li>
157:     <li>You can view and adjust the SQ's IP address in the <span class="naviSQ">Setup &gt; Network Setup</span> screen. If an address has been auto-assigned, this is denoted with an asterisk '(*)' after each value.</li>
158:     <li>When connected, the <strong>Lnk</strong> LED on the rear of the SQ will flash to show network activity.</li>
159:   </ul>
160:   <ul>
161:     <li>Connect the device running SQ MixPad to the same network, once again checking the IP range, but this time on your
162:       device.</li>
163:     <li>Setup the SQ with regards to mix-config, routing, and also ensure all remote audio units are connected.</li>
164:     <li>Open SQ MixPad and if everything is connected correctly you will see the SQ show up in the <span class="naviMP">Choose Unit</span> list*. Touch/click a unit to select it, then touch/click the <span class="naviMP">Connect</span> button.</li>
165:     <li>Select from the list of active users, enter the password (if one has been set) and touch/click the <span class="naviMP">Log In</span> button. (User Permissions and passwords are set using the SQ in the <span class="naviSQ">Setup &gt; Users</span> screen)</li>
166:     <li>Tick the <span class="naviMP">Remember Me</span> box to prevent the user list being displayed and a password being requested on subsequent
167:       logins. This only applies while the app is still running, restarting the app will always require a login.</li>
168:   </ul>
169:   <p>*The other two 'units' in the <span class="naviMP">Choose Unit</span> list are:</p>
170:   <ul>
171:     <li> <span class="naviMP">Offline</span> - Allows setup and show/scene/library management  without connection to an SQ console.</li>
